.TH "RPIMONITOR" "1" "Oct 18, 2026" "2.13" "RPi-Monitor"
.SH NAME
rpimonitor \- RPi-Monitor program
.SH COMMAND LINE
.sp
\fBrpimonitord\fP can be directly executed with the following parameters:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
rpimonitord [\-a address][ \-b pidfile][[\-c configuration_file]...][\-d delay][\-h][\-k][\-l logfile]
[\-m][\-n][\-p port][\-s][\-t timeout][\-v[v[...]]][\-V]
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Options
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-a,\-\-addr address
Web server bind address
Default: 0.0.0.0
.TP
.B \-b,\-\-background pid\-file
Define the pid file when run in background
Default: not set, application run in foreground
.TP
.B \-c,\-\-conf conf\-file
Define the configuration file
Default: \fB/etc/rpimonitor/data.conf\fP \fB/etc/rpimonitor/daemon.conf\fP
.TP
.B \-d,\-\-delay delay
Delay between check ins seconds
Default : 10
.TP
.B \-l,\-\-logfile log\-file
Logfile directory and prefix (ex: \fB/var/log/rpimonitor.log\fP)
Default: \fB/dev/null\fP
.TP
.B \-p,\-\-port port
Web server port
Default: 8888
.TP
.B \-t,\-\-timeout timeout
KPI read timeout in seconds
Default: 5
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBNote:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
If you want to change the default \fBdelay\fP, the rrd file will have to be deleted.
\fBrpimonitord\fP will recreate database at next startup with the new time slice.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-h,\-\-help
Shows this help and exit
.TP
.B \-i,\-\-interactive
Interactive configuration helper
.TP
.B \-k,\-\-keep
Keep log file (Default: logfile is delete at each start)
.TP
.B \-m,\-\-mib
Get MIB for current configuration
.TP
.B \-n,\-\-noserver
Don\(aqt start embeded web server
.TP
.B \-r,\-\-readonly
Read only mode.
.TP
.B \-s,\-\-show
Show configuration as loaded and exit
.TP
.B \-v,\-\-verbose
Write debug info on screen
.TP
.B \-V,\-\-Version
Show version and exit
.UNINDENT
.SH CONFIGURATION
.sp
Configuration can be defined into \fB/etc/rpimonitor/daemon.conf\fP and
\fB/etc/rpimonitor/data.conf\fP or in a list of files specified by \fB\-c\fP parameter.
.sp
In \fB/etc/rpimonitor/template/*.conf\fP, provided at installation, you can see
how to customize \fBrpimonitord\fP\&.
.sp
\fBNote:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Configuration defined inside a configuration file always overwrite default values.
.IP \(bu 2
Configuration given as command line option always overwrite values defined in files.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBWarning:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Be sure to use Linux filefeed format with line ending with LF (and not CR/LF like in Windows)
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBSee also:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
See configuration \%<20_index\:.html> chapter for details or usage \%<30_index\:.html> chapter for examples.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SH SNMP-AGENT
.sp
\fBrpimonitord\-snmp\fP is the snmp agent provided by \fBRPi\-Monitor\fP\&. This agent
allow \fBsnmpd\fP to access to data exctracted by \fBrpimonitord\fP\&.
.sp
\fBSee also:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
See configuration \%<20_index\:.html> chapter for details or usage \%<30_index\:.html> chapter for examples.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SH RAW DATA ACCESS
.sp
Once \fBrpimonitord\fP is started the data representing the current status are
available in json format and can be downloaded from the root of the web interface
(ex: \%<http://\:raspberrypi\:.local:8888>)
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBstatic.json\fP : Static information extracted at startup
.IP \(bu 2
\fBdynamic.json\fP : Current values of dynamic information extracted periodically
.IP \(bu 2
\fBmenu.json\fP : Description of menus when multiple pages are configured
.UNINDENT
.sp
The web interface configuration can also be downloaded in json format:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBstatistics.json\fP : Description of statistics page
.IP \(bu 2
\fBstatus.json\fP : Description of status page
.IP \(bu 2
\fBfriends.json\fP : List of friends
.IP \(bu 2
\fBaddons.json\fP : List of addons
.UNINDENT
.sp
Statistic information are stored into RRD file available in the directory \fB/var/lib/rpimonitor/stat/\fP
.SH STARTUP SCRIPT
.sp
\fBRPi\-Monitor\fP is configured to start automatically. \fB/etc/init.d/rpimonitor\fP
and link in runlevel startup directory (\fB/etc/rc?.d/\fP) do the job.
This script can be executed with the following parameters:
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B start
Start \fBrpimonitord\fP daemon
.TP
.B stop
Stop \fBrpimonitord\fP daemon
.TP
.B restart
Stop and start \fBrpimonitord\fP daemon
.TP
.B status
Show \fBrpimonitord\fP status
.TP
.B update
Update \(aqpackages to be installed\(aq list. This information is displayed in default
configuration of Web interface
.TP
.B install_auto_package_status_update
Add a script to automatically call package update script when \fBapt\fP commands are executed
.TP
.B remove_auto_package_status_update
Remove script automatically call for package update
.UNINDENT
